=== SURVEY ===
Mapped web `components/maps` + `motion`. Used the iOS17+/macOS14+ SwiftUI Map API (Map(position:)/Annotation/
MapPolyline/MapCircle/MapPolygon, MapContentBuilder) — available on the locked iOS18/macOS15 targets. Reused
TSChartPalette + P3-0003 playback (TSTimelineScrubber/TSPlaybackControls).

=== REASONING ===
- Geo logic is pure + unit-tested (TSGeo.isValid/boundingRegion/interpolate/routePosition) — coordinate
  validation rejects null-island (0,0); bounding region fits valid coords; routePosition interpolates playback.
- Native maps, no web behavior: TSMapView renders annotations + route polyline + geofence circles with .mapStyle;
  overlays exposed as @MapContentBuilder helpers (tsPolyline/tsCircle/tsRectangle/tsFeatureGroup) to embed in Map{}.
- Markers as content views (TSVehicleAnnotation/TSAnimatedMarker/TSMarkerCluster/TSCircleMarker); TSAnimatedMarker
  pulse + TSCarAnimation + TSFadeIn/Stagger/RouteTransition all gate animation on accessibilityReduceMotion.
- TSRoutePlayback drives an interpolated marker (TSGeo.routePosition) via a scrubber + transport controls + a
  cancellable .task ticker. Map carries an accessibilityLabel; geofence drawer lists overlays with radius.

